  "notes": "PoE, read 2026-11-28. `https://dl.ui.com/ds/usw-pro-24_ds.pdf` (HTTP 200, `application/pdf`, 415,079 B, text layer) prints **Networking interface = (24) GbE RJ45 ports / (2) 1/10G SFP+ ports**, **Power method = Universal input, 100-240V AC, 50/60 Hz; USP RPS DC input 11.5V DC, 2.61A**, **Power supply = AC/DC, internal, 36W** and **Max. power consumption = 30W**. No PoE line, no budget, no class: the non-PoE Switch Pro 24 is mains-powered, with the RPS DC bus as backup. Its 24 copper ports carry `poeIn: false` for the reason recorded in `usw-pro-48.json` - `isPoePd()` reads `unifi` out of the label and otherwise infers 12.95 W on each, 310.8 W of draw from a 30 W box."
